---
title: Smash Burgers
description: Double-stacked smash burgers with American cheese, pressed thin and crusted on a hot griddle.
tags: [sandwich, griddle]
course: main
icons: [burger-cheese, meat, salt-shaker]
cuisine: American
difficulty: easy
source:
  name: The Flat Top King
  author: Neal Williams
  url: https://theflattopking.com/blackstone-smash-burgers/
servings: 2
yield: 2%burgers
prep time: 10m
cook time: 5m
---

Preheat the #griddle{} on low until the surface reaches 425 to 450°F (220 to 230°C).

While it heats, divide the @ground beef chuck{3/4%lb}(12 to 14 oz, 80/20) into 4 equal portions and roll each one loosely into a ball between your palms.

> **Portioning** — A loosely packed 1/3 cup measure gives a ball of about 3 to 3 1/2 oz.

Get everything else ready too, because the cooking goes fast. Unwrap the @American cheese{4%slices}, put the @burger seasoning{}(or salt and pepper) within reach, and set out your toppings, such as mayonnaise, yellow mustard, dill pickles, and tomato slices.

Set the beef balls on the hottest part of the griddle, leaving room between them to smash and flip.

Working quickly, lay a piece of #parchment paper{} over a ball and press down with a #burger press{} or stiff spatula until the patty is thin and even. Keep the pressure on for about ~hold{10%seconds}, then repeat with the other balls.

Season the top of each patty with the burger seasoning. Only this side gets seasoned.

Dab the cut sides of the @hamburger buns{2} in the grease on the griddle and toast them while the burgers cook. Pull the buns off once toasted and dress them with your condiments.

When the patties are a little more than halfway cooked, with a few pink spots still showing on top, flip them with a #spatula{}. Scrape underneath so the crust comes up with the patty instead of staying on the griddle.

Immediately lay a slice of cheese on each patty.

As soon as the cheese melts, likely in under a minute, stack the patties in pairs to make two double burgers. Take them off the griddle right away, set them on the buns, and serve warm.
